  "findings": [
    "The fixed runtime defaults Flash Attention to auto. Quantized V with auto is explicitly changed to enabled; q8 V is not evidence that Flash Attention was disabled.",
    "CPU tiled prefill and split-KV decode fast paths require K/V with equal types, either F16 or F32, plus their other shape/reference-path conditions. Q8_0 does not meet these predicates; its one-chunk fallback still calls vector dot products and must not be labelled no-SIMD.",
    "The model header has 28 layers, 8 KV heads and 128 dimensions each for K and V. One 16384-token cache body at two bytes per element requires 1879048192 bytes. This excludes model weights, graph/work buffers, process overhead and allocator effects.",
    "Common application info is verbosity 3, but the callback maps GGML/llama INFO to trace level 4. Explicit verbosity 4 permits the backend loader and attention-configuration INFO records suppressed by the earlier threshold."
  ],
  "cache_body_estimate": {
    "layers": 28,
    "tokens": 16384,
    "parallel_slots": 1,
    "kv_heads": 8,
    "key_dimensions": 128,
    "value_dimensions": 128,
    "f16_bytes_per_element": 2,
    "formula": "28 * 16384 * 8 * (128 + 128) * 2",
